  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday) \nIssued at 923 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nA Fall-like weather pattern will persist through the long term\nperiod as the Tennessee Valley sits underneath northwest flow that\nwill continue to usher in a cooler airmass. Dry conditions \ncontinue with afternoon highs in the low to mid 80s with overnight\nlows in the mid to upper 50s. As we head into next week, a weak\nmid level ridge begins to shift into the Southeast. This should\nwarm temperatures up a few degrees into the mid to upper 80s. At\nthe same time a shortwave is forecast to dig southeast across the\nPlains. This would bring a low chance of precip during the day on\nMonday. However, this is quite far out and at this time there is\nlow confidence in this occurring. Therefore, kept the NBM very \nlow chance (5-15%) of showers on Monday.",
